<Project>

  <!--
    Vixen — the in-process application host of docs/plan/12 § "Test infrastructure worth building
    early", linked rather than referenced, on the same argument as Vixen.Testing.props beside it.

    A THIRD FILE for the same reason RecordingBackend has a second one: the split is by what the file
    needs, not by what it is for. TestApp.cs names Game, VixenApp, HeadlessPlatform, MemoryFileProvider
    and NullDevice, so linking it anywhere else is a build error in return for nothing.

    Consumers need a `using Vixen.Testing;`, xunit.v3, and a reference that brings in Tools/Vixen.App
    — which carries Vixen.App.Hosting, Vixen.Platform.Headless and Vixen.Graphics.Null with it, and is
    the whole set of projects that could host an application anyway.
  -->

  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)TestApp.cs" Link="Testing\TestApp.cs" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
